# The climbing scene: a walker walks to a wall, climbs it, crosses its top and climbs down the far side, then turns
# round where it stands. Checks which way the waist bends at the corners (the gaster should stay along the floor at the
# foot of the wall and hang over the top edge) and that the legs step when it turns on the spot.
# The wall is a pillar one block wide, so the camera beside it sees the ant's side straight on (a long wall's near end
# looks far bigger than the stone by the ant, which makes heights hard to judge), and a gaster in the stone would hide.
# The turn from three-quarters is drawn 3 times a tick ("frames 3"), as a fast screen shows it between ticks.
# Run: ./gradlew runFilm -PfilmScene=tools/film/climb.film   Pictures, climb.txt, turn.txt and checks.txt:
# run-film/screenshots/climb/
cmd time set noon
cmd weather clear
cmd fill 3 -60 -4 3 -59 4 air
cmd fill 3 -60 0 3 -59 0 stone
lens 30
walker worker_ant 1.5 -60 0.5 -90
camera 1.0 -59.0 -3.5 -20 25
shot climb_scene
log climb
cmd tick freeze
fov 10
follow 0 0.15 -7 0 0
go 3 -58 0
burst up 60 1
go 6 -60 0
burst down 70 1
log off
log turn
fov 30
follow 0 1.9 0 0 90
look 0 -60 0.5
burst turn_above 30 1
look off
follow 0.65 0.55 0.65 135 30
look 12 -60 0.5
frames 3
burst turn_34 30 1
frames 1
look off
log off
follow off
quit
